    "turn_text": "No, yeah, I mean, if we fought it for years, I'm trying to get medical waivers from viewers, people being the bureau of medical personnel for the Navy. And yeah, they're just not very flexible. So I've actually created a, I've got it signed in law and an NDAA that the, you know, he does have to look at. creating career pathways for people like me who don't want to be medically retired but have the experience that is still useful to the military. We've already got enough people that are trying to get medically retired for some bullshit and just to get benefits for the rest of their lives and then you have another subset of people who never wanted to be medically retired but they kind of have to be. So that was, I mean, I could have been limited, what's called limited duty, but then you can't deploy, and you can't deploy, like there's really a ceiling to your, you're not gonna get promoted, you're not gonna become Admiral McCraven. So, you know, what's the point? And so, yeah, in a sense, it was kind of forcibly moved out, and yeah, it was sad for us. We loved our life.",
