    "turn_text": "um, but I did my master's in public life. I wanted to stay in national security policy and then I was trying to figure out what that meant. So, you know, graduated and was just mucking around DC for a while, had a seal buddy who got me in touch with Congressman Pete Sessions, actually, he just gave me an intern badge to really just network. And so I would, you know, take meetings and just kind of figure out like what that next step is. One of those meetings with the staff, staffer who worked for Senator Cotton at the time, He's like, I don't know, your resume seems like you should just run for Congress. Why are you looking for jobs? And I was like, oh yeah, just run for Congress, just like that. And it's not like we never thought about it. I mean, you're familiar with the Kennedy School. They're trying to train politicians there.",
