  {
    "episode_id": 90392,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90392.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 114,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. I mean, where do we begin? Social media is on net. It doesn't seem to be a good for humanity. Like any new communication method, humanity needs some time to figure it out and adapt our brains to it. You know, that was true of the printing press. It's true of written language. It's true of many things. And so, but social media is, I mean, it's all that, but on steroids, and it kind of puts the world in front of you. in a very intense way. And I don't care who you are, you're not emotionally capable of dealing with that. There's somebody said, and I'm just gonna start stealing the quote instead of giving it to somebody, but I did hear it from somebody else. I'm like, only God is emotionally capable of dealing with omniscience. You are not. The social media, you know, it sort of, it gives you a glimpse into omniscience in a way, because it's sort of like, if you're really deep diving, you see everything going on around the world and your psyche is, of course, gravitates towards negativity. That's a normal human psychological phenomenon. And it kind of makes you crazy, you know, and sometimes that people are",
