  {
    "episode_id": 90392,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90392.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 116,
    "turn_text": "I'm losing everything, everything's going to shit. And I'm like, whoa, get offline. Just get offline for 30 days, go talk to your people in your community, and I think you're gonna be like, okay, we're normal. It's fine. But the other bad aspects of it are, it creates a sense that I think the extremes of both sides are more powerful than they really are. And that begins to affect another subset of the population that's, I think, susceptible to those voices. Otherwise, they would be kind of looking at their more regular sources of information, but instead get their sources from the comment section. I mean, the thing that people believe about me, like, I'd laugh at it if it wasn't so disconcerting. It's just endless. I mean, I'm talking about this from my own side. The left hates me for whatever reason. But that's kind of how it's supposed to be. We're supposed to have a left-right dichotomy. That's OK. You want it to be fact-based and rational. But in the end, that's OK. That's kind of the point of politics. What's become different, I think, since the 2018 time frame and the advent of the squad on the left, and then I maybe take some blame for this because I was one of the first to really really use social media in a very heavy way as a Republican. And then I think others maybe thought they were following in my footsteps, but not so much. Because again, I try to entertain you in order to bring you into a serious discussion. I understand what social media can do, but you've got to still tell the truth and bring people into a rational place. And what it's become is the opposite. And I told my voters close time, like, don't be easy to lie to. It's really easy to tell you what you want to hear. You got to be more skeptical of people telling you, like singing from the same sheet of music. And, you know, the squad opened that up for the left in a really, really profound way. Hasn't done them any good.",
