    "turn_idx": 197,
    "turn_text": "So let me ask you about, you say one of the fights that you fought was last year, And you've been very consistent on the border. Senator Langford, Senator Murphy, Republican Democrat, agreed on a bill that was indisputably the toughest bill that we've seen on border enforcement in a very long time. President agreed to it. It looked like it was going to pass in the Senate, probably in the House as well. And then it was It was set aside after Trump said that Republicans shouldn't pass it. And one of the things he said was it would help Biden, it would help the Democrats to pass this bill. That has to run counter to your view of politics, the way politics should be. You don't delay a solution for a year because you think that it would put you at a political disadvantage if you believe what you say that this is a critical problem.",
